[
    {
        "content": "<p>In CGT we've had the problem that the simp-normal form of <code>↑{x | p x}</code> is <code>{ x // p x }</code>, but typeclasses about <code>↑s</code> don't apply to <code>{ x // p x }</code>. Should <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.coe_setOf#doc\">docs#Set.coe_setOf</a> be un-simped?</p>",
        "id": 579578323,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773612143
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Which type classes are affected?</p>",
        "id": 579578773,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773612465
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In CGT it was with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Small#doc\">docs#Small</a>, but I imagine it's the case for anything that has a <code>↑s</code> in a type field where you can insert a <code>{x | p x}</code> for the <code>s</code>.</p>",
        "id": 579578854,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773612535
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I wonder if adding the same instances for subtypes is a feasible alternative</p>",
        "id": 579578971,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1773612621
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I also completely don't see the point of having this simp lemma</p>",
        "id": 579579049,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773612666
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>what does it even do for you</p>",
        "id": 579579055,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773612672
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So where is the PR removing it? :-)</p>",
        "id": 579579355,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773612920
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh sure I can make one soon</p>",
        "id": 579579409,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773612958
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another alternative here would be to make the coercion instance_reducible</p>",
        "id": 579580619,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773613992
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is probably a good idea anyway, I don't see why we'd want <code>{x | p x}</code> and <code>{x // p x}</code> to ever have different instances</p>",
        "id": 579580630,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773614014
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Wait, it already is reducible!</p>",
        "id": 579580669,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773614060
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/.60Set.2Ecoe_setOf.60/near/579578323\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>but typeclasses about <code>↑s</code> don't apply to <code>{ x // p x }</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Which ones do you have in mind?</p>",
        "id": 579580695,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773614088
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>specifically it was <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=small_sep#doc\">docs#small_sep</a> with <a href=\"https://vihdzp.github.io/combinatorial-games/find/?pattern=Surreal.small_setOf_birthday_lt#doc\">CGT#Surreal.small_setOf_birthday_lt</a></p>",
        "id": 579581364,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773614756
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it didn't work with just <a href=\"https://vihdzp.github.io/combinatorial-games/find/?pattern=Surreal.small_subtype_birthday_lt#doc\">CGT#Surreal.small_subtype_birthday_lt</a></p>",
        "id": 579581425,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773614800
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Duplicating small_sep for subtype would presumably suffice here?</p>",
        "id": 579581523,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773614903
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think making set a one-field structure would help here, since then <code>setOf</code> could be safely made instance reducible</p>",
        "id": 579581623,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1773614981
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>sorry, to clarify:<br>\nthe typeclass goal is <code>Small.{u, u + 1} ↑{x : Surreal | x.birthday &lt; o}</code>, but <a href=\"https://vihdzp.github.io/combinatorial-games/find/?pattern=Surreal.small_subtype_birthday_lt#doc\">CGT#Surreal.small_subtype_birthday_lt</a> isn't applying to it</p>",
        "id": 579581768,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773615115
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this goal is coming from the typeclass assumption in <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=small_sep#doc\">docs#small_sep</a></p>",
        "id": 579581811,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773615160
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm somewhat surprised that <code>{x // p x}</code> isn't just notation for <code>↑{x | p x}</code></p>",
        "id": 579581837,
        "sender_full_name": "Violeta Hernández",
        "timestamp": 1773615178
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>Subtype</code> is in core, <code>Set</code> is in Mathlib<br>\nAlso <code>Subtype</code>s are useful</p>",
        "id": 579581959,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1773615265
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/.60Set.2Ecoe_setOf.60/near/579579409\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>oh sure I can make one soon</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>it didn't work :(</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- from Mathlib.Data.Set.Finite</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Powerset</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe_setOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Type mismatch: After simplification, term</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  h_eq</span>\n<span class=\"sd\"> has type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  ⟨s i, ⋯⟩ = ⟨s j, ⋯⟩</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">but is expected to have type</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  s i = s j</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">infinite_iUnion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Infinite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Injective</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⋃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Infinite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hfin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">not_injective_infinite_finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hfin</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">finite_subsets</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">to_subtype</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">subset_iUnion</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_⟩</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_eq</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 579602517,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773627927
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it works if you add <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code> <span aria-label=\"smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f604\" role=\"img\" title=\"smile\">:smile:</span></p>\n<p>(I'm still kind of confused about that option... is the idea that we deprecated some overly expensive simplification/rewriting behavior and now code is breaking which happened to depend on that behavior?)</p>",
        "id": 579612179,
        "sender_full_name": "Matt Diamond",
        "timestamp": 1773636304
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It used to be that, when typechecking the implicit arguments of functions, Lean would bump the transparency level, so Lean was willing to unfold default transparency functions. This was expensive and unpredictable. Now we only unfold things marked <code>@[reducible]</code>, or the new <code>@[implicit_reducible]</code> level, in this situation.</p>\n<p>Mathlib had <em>thoroughly</em> taken advantage of this \"feature\", and we're now facing the consequences.</p>",
        "id": 579614152,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773637756
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is a new tool <code>#defeq_abuse in</code>, which you can put before a declaration, which hopefully will give you some useful feedback about what is going wrong that requires <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code> (and PRs <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36706\">#36706</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36701\">#36701</a> add more features to this).</p>\n<p>People working on leaves of Mathlib are welcome to add the option as needed to avoid getting too bogged down, but we have a massive technical debt here to pay off, and <em>everyone</em> is invited to run <code>#defeq_abuse</code> and to help resolve these problems.</p>",
        "id": 579614254,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1773637861
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The problem is that <code>a ∈ {x | p x} ↔ p a</code> is not defeq under <code>implicit_reducible</code>. Making <code>Set</code> a one-field structure would fix this.</p>",
        "id": 579656258,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1773654419
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hopefully <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41506\">#41506</a> will fix this problem once and for all</p>",
        "id": 613326415,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1785293253
    }
]